:32:24Z", "body": "I'll revert"}, {"id": 1123193599, "in_reply_to_id": 1122567877, "path": "api/src/main/java/com/microsoft/gctoolkit/jvm/AbstractJavaVirtualMachine.java", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T14:33:33Z", "body": "yuck!"}, {"id": 1123208307, "in_reply_to_id": 1122567687, "path": "api/pom.xml", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T14:42:36Z", "body": "using ${revision} from mvn version 3.5.0+"}, {"id": 1123303207, "in_reply_to_id": 1122567176, "path": "IT/pom.xml", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T15:39:52Z", "body": "revised to using the revision mechanism (https://maven.apache.org/maven-ci-friendly.html) "}, {"id": 1123312815, "in_reply_to_id": 1122568022, "path": "api/src/main/java/com/microsoft/gctoolkit/jvm/AbstractJavaVirtualMachine.java", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T15:45:49Z", "body": "Tricky.. If the property is set one shouldn't have to set anything else. But, this should be part of a larger conversation about tag vs level based logging."}, {"id": 1123319006, "in_reply_to_id": 1122568561, "path": "api/src/test/java/com/microsoft/gctoolkit/time/DateTimeStampTest.java", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T15:49:46Z", "body": "I think this has now been resolved..."}, {"id": 1123319414, "in_reply_to_id": 1122568658, "path": "gclogs/pom.xml", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T15:50:02Z", "body": "done"}, {"id": 1123319904, "in_reply_to_id": 1122568715, "path": "parser/pom.xml", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T15:50:21Z", "body": "done"}, {"id": 1123322415, "in_reply_to_id": 1122568819, "path": "parser/src/test/java/com/microsoft/gctoolkit/parser/unittests/UnifiedGenerationalParserTest.java", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T15:51:58Z", "body": "testForCMSLogsMissingTimestamps(....  maybe ;-)"}, {"id": 1123453981, "in_reply_to_id": null, "path": "IT/pom.xml", "user": "dsgrieve", "created_at": "2023-03-02T17:13:15Z", "body": "I think you want to back this out. The version should be automagically updated by the release process. "}, {"id": 1123462436, "in_reply_to_id": 1122567687, "path": "api/pom.xml", "user": "dsgrieve", "created_at": "2023-03-02T17:18:39Z", "body": "I think you want to back this change out. The release should take care of updating the version. "}, {"id": 1123536942, "in_reply_to_id": null, "path": "api/src/main/java/com/microsoft/gctoolkit/time/DateTimeStamp.java", "user": "dsgrieve", "created_at": "2023-03-02T18:18:06Z", "body": "This doesn't seem right. I think you may be counting the offset twice under certain circumstances. If the DateTimeStamp has both date and time stamps, then you will have adjusted the timeStamp by the offset and the dateStamp by the offset. "}, {"id": 1123538353, "in_reply_to_id": null, "path": "api/src/test/java/com/microsoft/gctoolkit/time/DateTimeStampTest.java", "user": "dsgrieve", "created_at": "2023-03-02T18:19:24Z", "body": "The fact that you changed this test case means you changed the behavior of DateTimeStamp. This is a breaking change. "}, {"id": 1123546592, "in_reply_to_id": null, "path": "api/src/test/java/com/microsoft/gctoolkit/time/DateTimeStampTest.java", "user": "dsgrieve", "created_at": "2023-03-02T18:26:44Z", "body": "I think you should leave this test in, especially since the compareTo implementation hasn't changed (it should still throw an IllegalStateException). This will help flag possible changes in behavior down the road. "}, {"id": 1123547203, "in_reply_to_id": null, "path": "api/src/test/java/com/microsoft/gctoolkit/time/DateTimeStampTest.java", "user": "dsgrieve", "created_at": "2023-03-02T18:27:21Z", "body": "I think these should be left in as well. "}, {"id": 1123547518, "in_reply_to_id": null, "path": "gclogs/pom.xml", "user": "dsgrieve", "created_at": "2023-03-02T18:27:43Z", "body": "Back this change out."}, {"id": 1123549161, "in_reply_to_id": null, "path": "parser/pom.xml", "user": "dsgrieve", "created_at": "2023-03-02T18:29:19Z", "body": "Back this change out. "}, {"id": 1123549841, "in_reply_to_id": null, "path": "pom.xml", "user": "dsgrieve", "created_at": "2023-03-02T18:29:51Z", "body": "Back this change out"}, {"id": 1123550113, "in_reply_to_id": null, "path": "sample/pom.xml", "user": "dsgrieve", "created_at": "2023-03-02T18:30:09Z", "body": "Back this change out"}, {"id": 1123550591, "in_reply_to_id": null, "path": "vertx/pom.xml", "user": "dsgrieve", "created_at": "2023-03-02T18:30:38Z", "body": "Back this change out"}, {"id": 1123624528, "in_reply_to_id": 1123453981, "path": "IT/pom.xml", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T19:48:05Z", "body": "this has been backed out.."}, {"id": 1123635011, "in_reply_to_id": 1123538353, "path": "api/src/test/java/com/microsoft/gctoolkit/time/DateTimeStampTest.java", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T19:59:56Z", "body": "I did change the behaviour but it isn't a breaking change AFAIK. The issues is what to do with logs that don't have a timestamp. Since there is (historically) a lot of behaviour that is based on the presence of a time stamp, not having a timestamp wasn't a viable option. To fix this the time in seconds from epoc is offered as a timestamp. About the only thing that affects is timestamp is consider to be the age of the JVM. However, given we have to deal with log fragements anyways, and date stamps don't give us the age of the JVM implies that using epoc as a starting point seems like a pragmatic solution.\r\n\r\nThe better way to manage IMO is to encapsulate *all* of the time calculations into DateTimeStamp. However, that would trigger another massive refactoring of all client code. I personally have no appetite for this at the moment."}, {"id": 1123647143, "in_reply_to_id": 1123536942, "path": "api/src/main/java/com/microsoft/gctoolkit/time/DateTimeStamp.java", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T20:14:15Z", "body": "Yes, the date stamp will be adjusted along with the date stamp. Maybe more documentation is needed here.\r\nThe time stamp is the age of the JVM (unless not set). Date stamp is the calendar time. Both need to be adjust to keep them coherent."}, {"id": 1123648848, "in_reply_to_id": 1123547203, "path": "api/src/test/java/com/microsoft/gctoolkit/time/DateTimeStampTest.java", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T20:16:19Z", "body": "I could be wrong but I don't think these tests make sense with the change in implementation. "}, {"id": 1123648965, "in_reply_to_id": 1123547518, "path": "gclogs/pom.xml", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T20:16:29Z", "body": "done"}, {"id": 1123649031, "in_reply_to_id": 1123549161, "path": "parser/pom.xml", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T20:16:35Z", "body": "done"}, {"id": 1123649127, "in_reply_to_id": 1123549841, "path": "pom.xml", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T20:16:42Z", "body": "done"}, {"id": 1123649218, "in_reply_to_id": 1123550113, "path": "sample/pom.xml", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T20:16:50Z", "body": "done"}, {"id": 1123649308, "in_reply_to_id": 1123550591, "path": "vertx/pom.xml", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T20:16:58Z", "body": "done"}, {"id": 1123655588, "in_reply_to_id": 1122568022, "path": "api/src/main/java/com/microsoft/gctoolkit/jvm/AbstractJavaVirtualMachine.java", "user": null, "created_at": "2023-03-02T20:24:36Z", "body": "I think this is part of a larger discussion of tags vs levels. My intent in Censum/GCToolKit was to build up a tag based logging framework. This is "}]}